  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nFollowing the discussion in https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/7233, I understand why JSON modules don't have a `script` destination. However, it's unclear to me why they should have a destination different from regular `fetch` (i.e. the empty string, or`Sec-Fetch-Dest: empty`. Seems like imported json modules are no different from calling `(await fetch()).json()` ?\r\n\r\nThis means, for example, that you need to preload the same JSON file differently if you use it in a `fetch` vs if you use it in an `import`, and that doesn't seem right.\r\n\r\n@nicolo-ribaudo @annevk \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
